-- lib/paper.cub — a paper as one value of the language (Avik, 2026-11-15: "ONE SOURCE OF INFORMATION";
-- "Nothing is ever allowed to be stale"). The paper exists once, as a value of type Paper; every
-- presentation of it is a projection computed from that value (here `human`, the manuscript as it
-- reads), and none is stored beside it. A block is a stretch of the manuscript between blank lines:
-- a heading, English prose, a displayed construction (mathematics or code), or a note to the reader
-- of the source. A construction the paper states is realized by code: `realized` holds a block and the
-- names of the definitions that are its code (each a definition of docs/hyperactivity.cub, its type the
-- construction's statement, named by section and equation: eq-1-2 for (1.2)); the names are checked
-- to name definitions when the paper is kept in the store (lib/paper-view.cub; hyperactive check
-- reports each name no file the machine has read declares). Avik, 2026-11-15: the
-- source holds each construction as code with the English attached; the pure page is the projection
-- of the code and its naming words, the human paper the projection with all the English.
import "selection.hypercubical"
